  "id": "exogenous-attention",
  "term": "exogenous attention",
  "definition": "Exogenous attention is attention that is automatically drawn by outside stimuli, especially negative or threatening ones. In this source, it refers to the way fear- and disgust-related distractors capture attention, with these emotions affecting attention at different points in time.",
